    "lawSection": "Livingston County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5362\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize the funding of the sanitary sewer system in the\nhamlet of Hemlock in the town of Livonia\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill will legalize and validate certain minor technical\nviolations of the Local Finance Law by the Town of Livonia in\nconnection with the issuance of bond anticipation notes to finance\nsanitary sewer improvements within the town, thereby validating\ncertain bond anticipation notes and authorizing the town to issue\nfurther bond anticipation notes and/or bonds in order to finance the\nproject.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill is a special act which legalizes, validates, ratifies and\nconfirms certain actions and proceedings taken by the Town of Livonia,\nLivingston County, from March 21, 2002 to date with connection with\nthe adoption of a serial bond resolution and issuance of certain bond\nanticipation notes of the town. The bill specifically provides that\nnotwithstanding specific technical violations of certain provisions of\nthe Local Finance Law, the bond resolution adopted by the town in\n2002, together with certain bond anticipation notes issued by the town\nare legal and valid obligations of the town.  The bill also further\nauthorizes the town to issue renewal bond anticipation notes and or\nserial bonds in order to complete the financing of the project.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Town of Livonia adopted a serial bond resolution in 2002 for\npurposes of financing certain sanitary sewer improvements.\nUnfortunately, after the adoption of the bond resolution, certain bond\nanticipation notes were issued by the town and thereafter renewed by\nthe town in a fashion which, in certain cases, were in technical\nviolation of certain provisions of the Local Finance Law. The\nviolations included the length of the issuance of bond anticipation\nnotes and the failure to redeem a portion of such bond anticipation\nnotes within two years of original date of issuance of the bond\nanticipation notes.\n\nThe Town of Livonia is in the process of attempting to refinance the\noutstanding obligations through the Environmental Facilities\nCorporation on very beneficial terms to the town.  Unfortunately, the\ntown cannot go forward with this financing unless the technical\ndefects in the original obligations are validated by the Legislature.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nChapter 679, Laws of 2006 (S.6944-A/A.10216-A).\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThe Town of Livonia may be able to save significant interest costs as\na result of this legislation and will be able to renew certain\noutstanding bond anticipation notes.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
